From 6fcc431b73668c1e816eda0dd2877ba2e3272cd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Heimes <cheimes@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2015 13:46:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Python 3 migration: modernize code for 2/3 compatibility

Run python-modernize on code base:
  python-modernize --write --nobackups \
    pylint-build-scan.py \
    base/server/python/ \
    base/server/python/pki/server/deployment/scriptlets/*.py \
    base/common/python/ \
    base/kra/functional/ \
    tests/dogtag/ \
    base/common/sbin/pki-upgrade \
    base/server/sbin/pkidestroy \
    base/server/sbin/pkispawn \
    base/server/sbin/pki-server \
    base/server/sbin/pki-server-upgrade \
    base/java-tools/bin/pki \
    $(find base/common/upgrade/ -type f -name '[0-9]*') \
    $(find base/server/upgrade/ -type f -name '[0-9]*')

Manual fixes after modernize:
  Move __future__ imports below shebang lines
  Remove import of types module
  Silence pylint warnings about six.move

Add six to requirements

Use six.iteritems(attr_list) instead of list(attr_list.items())

Improve pylint integration

Handle additional differences between Python 2 and 3:
    Exceptions have no 'message' attribute, use str(e) instead.
    Fix imports of urllib.quote() and urlparse().
    Reorder shutil.Error and OSerror. shutil.Error is now a subclass
       of OSError.
    Don't use the exceptions module.
